00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.000
Get your pencils and get the lead out.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.000
Get ready to take down this number that I'm going to give you,

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.000
which I will give you in just a few minutes.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.000
Now you can write for this book.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:13.000
It's a book on a new game called Pedestrian Polo.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:17.000
We'll give you the rules and all of the principles of the game

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:21.000
as soon as we tell you a few of the things that you have to look out for.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:22.000
There are different types of pedestrians.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:27.000
First we have the out-of-towners, who comes into town and they wait for the light to change,

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:32.000
and finally decides that he won't cross because of the traffic, and he goes the other way.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:35.000
Down the block about nine times, and he never gets anywhere.

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.000
In fact, he shouldn't have even come to town.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:43.000
The writer that wrote that shouldn't have even handed it in.

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:49.000
Now we have a fellow that starts out here who is anxious to get over to Joe's place, and he jaywalks.

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:53.000
And after he comes out of jaywalks, he becomes an S-Walker.

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:59.000
Now an S-Walker is a man who walks like that, and then goes back over to Joe's place.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:06.000
Now to be able to be a good pedestrian, you must be able to jump three ways at the same time.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:10.000
There's another writer that did that.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:15.000
Now the one thing that you must always remember when you're driving, especially.

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.000
Now there are different types of new things coming out every day.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:21.000
We have the new bumper that has the rubber stamp on the front of it.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:25.000
When you hit a pedestrian, it says, kill in this town.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.000
Another thing we have is the floorboards.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:31.000
It's made out of glass so that you can apologize to the pedestrian after you've run over him.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:34.000
You must be sporty about this game at all times.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:39.000
Now there is three lights, the traffic lights, that are very important in this game.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:45.000
Now first is the red light, and then the orange light, and the green light.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:48.000
Now the...

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:53.000
Well it looks like it's green anyhow. I'm color blind, it don't make any difference.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:57.000
Anyhow, now the idea is, the principle of these lights is,

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:04.000
when the green light is on, and the orange light comes on, that means go fast so you won't hit the red one.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:10.000
Now, there are different types of rules that you must follow at all times, and playing pedestrian polo.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:13.000
First, the pedestrian.

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.000
However be too kind, no pedestrian.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:18.000
If you see one, get him.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:22.000
Now this is open season, and we have a score.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:26.000
If you hit a man, that is five points.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:29.000
If you hit a woman, that is fifteen points.

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:33.000
If you're carrying a baby, you add a half a point.

00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:41.000
Now, the other day I hit a guy who was wearing a pant, but I didn't know what the score was.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.000
I don't think he did either.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:49.000
Now if you hit a man and knock him down in a sewer, that's a hole in one.

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:53.000
If you knock him through the air, knock him over fifty feet, that's called a birdie.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:59.000
Now, one of the most important things to remember while playing pedestrian polo is to keep your windshield clean.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:02.000
Because you may miss a pedestrian completely.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.000
This is very heartbreaking, you know.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:07.000
Now I suggest that you would use Tide.

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:10.000
Tide is very wonderful for washing all glassware.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:14.000
This, by the way, if you haven't figured out, is the commercial part now.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:18.000
This is the side of a window that has been washed with Tide, and this side has not.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:22.000
You can see the difference.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:24.000
There's a glass in there.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:26.000
Now get ready to take this number down.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.000
I'm going to give it to you any minute now.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.000
I'm going to give you the number.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.000
I can't give it to you just now.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:34.000
Now, one thing I'd like to call your attention to is what the safety zones are for.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:38.000
That's in case you hit somebody outside of them that don't count.

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:45.000
If someone steps out of the safety zone, knock them back in before you get out.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:49.000
Now, a lot of accidents are caused because people really don't know how to drive.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:56.000
Now, coming down here tonight, there was a car in front of me, and I'll tell you, this poor soul didn't know what she was doing.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.000
It was an out-of-towner.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.000
You can tell by the license plate.

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:01.000
We come to this red light, a stop light.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.000
She stopped.

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.000
How do you like that?

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.000
Now, I'd like to call your attention to some of the things about Tide.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:13.000
Now, Tide has a new bumper that we're putting out now, a Tide bumper that has a brush in it.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:19.000
This is so when you hit a pedestrian, it sprinkles a little Tide over them, and then a can of water comes out and sprinkles the pedestrian,

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:22.000
and they get so mad when you knock them down and they get dirty.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:27.000
This way, they'll get up and thank you for knocking them down.

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:34.000
Now, Tide is also – here's a car before it was washed with Tide, and here is the same car after it had been washed.

00:17:34.000 --> 00:17:41.000
If you're very much interested in this, I would like to call your attention, not only does Tide get clothes cleaner than any soap,

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:49.000
not only does it get glassware sparkling bright, but it gets wash prints dazzling bright, and now we have – what's this?

